{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5977,
  "title": "Check that esbuild, Vite and webpack 4/5 apps can bundle and render Web Chat",
  "body": "> Nothing checks that apps can bundle Web Chat: `import('react-dom/client')` breaks webpack 5 on React 16.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Added\n\n- 👷🏻 Pull request validation: added rendering Web Chat bundled by esbuild, Vite, webpack 4 and 5 with React 16, 18 and 19\n- Docs: added [workarounds for webpack 4](./docs/HOSTING.md#bundling-with-webpack-4)\n\n### Changed\n\n- `botframework-webchat-core` connects to Redux DevTools without the `@redux-devtools/extension` package\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed webpack 4 failing to resolve `botframework-webchat/schema.js` and `@redux-devtools/extension`\n\n## Description\n\nA new job builds an app per bundler from the tarballs on React 16, 18 or 19 and checks it renders in Chrome.\n\nWeb Chat ships a root `schema.js` and drops `@redux-devtools/extension`: webpack 4 only needs Babel.\n\n## Design\n\n- Apps set up as in their bundler's docs; Chrome 141 runs in a Selenium Docker image, driven over WebDriver.\n- `createStore` reads the DevTools extension's global like Redux Toolkit, not breaking.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `pull-request-validation.yml`: `bundler-test` job, 12 legs\n- `__tests__/bundlers/<bundler>/`: the apps (React 16 uses `ReactDOM.render`); `run.mjs` checks them in the `Dockerfile`'s Chrome; `HOSTING.md` has webpack 4's config\n- `bundle/schema.js`: shim like `decorator.js`\n- `createStore.ts`: reads `__REDUX_DEVTOOLS_EXTENSION_COMPOSE__`, has a spec\n- `directlinespeech/babel.config.json`: test build uses release targets\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
  "author": {
    "login": "OEvgeny",
    "type": "User",
